; OpTypeVectorIdEXT: Component Count is treated as an unsigned value and must
; be greater than zero. When the count is a specialization constant, this can
; only be checked after the value is translated. Here the default (7) is valid
; but a -spec-const override to 0 must be rejected by the reverse translator.

; RUN: not llvm-spirv -spirv-text -r -spec-const "42:i32:0" %s -o %t.bc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

; CHECK: InvalidInstruction
; CHECK: TypeVectorIdEXT: component count must be greater than zero

119734787 66304 458752 10 0
2 Capability Addresses
2 Capability Linkage
2 Capability Kernel
6 Extension "SPV_EXT_long_vector"
3 MemoryModel 2 2
3 Source 3 102000
4 Name 1 "test"

6 Decorate 1 LinkageAttributes "test" Export
4 Decorate 2 SpecId 42
4 TypeInt 4 32 0
4 SpecConstant 4 2 7
2 TypeVoid 3
3 TypeFloat 5 32
4 TypeVectorIdEXT 6 5 2
4 TypeFunction 7 3 6

5 Function 3 1 0 7
3 FunctionParameter 6 8

2 Label 9
1 Return

1 FunctionEnd
